{
  "slug": "ido4specs",
  "name": "Ido4specs",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "ido4specs is the bridge between a strategic spec and GitHub issues. It analyzes your codebase, decomposes capabilities into implementation tasks with effort, risk, type, and dependency metadata, and produces a structurally-validated technical spec any downstream tool can consume.\n\nKey features:\n- Code-grounded decomposition - parallel Explore subagents ground every task in concrete files, services, and patterns from your actual codebase (not fabricated from the spec)\n- Structured output enforced by a bundled zero-dependency parser - every task carries effort (S/M/L/XL), risk (low → critical), type (feature/infrastructure), AI-suitability (full/assisted/pair/human), and dependency graph\n- Two-layer validation - deterministic structural parser + independent qualitative review before handoff\n\nBuilt for tech leads, staff engineers, and founder-engineers who want to skip the manual decomposition tax.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **8 skills**, **3 agents** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (8): `create-spec` (Phase 1 — strategic spec + codebase → technical canvas), `doctor` (Diagnostic checks for the ido4specs plugin), `help` (Explains what ido4specs does, what skills are available, how the pipeline works, and how to get started), `refine-spec` (Edits an existing technical spec artifact using natural-language instructions), `review-spec` (Runs a qualitative review of a technical spec artifact — two-stage protocol (format compliance then content quality) applied…), `spec-quality` (Specification quality standards for technical specs), `synthesize-spec` (Phase 2 — technical canvas → technical spec artifact), `validate-spec` (Validates a technical spec artifact for format compliance and content quality)\n- **Agents** (3): `code-analyzer` (Canvas template and rules reference for the /ido4specs:create-spec skill), `spec-reviewer` (Review protocol and rules reference for the /ido4specs:review-spec skill), `technical-spec-writer` (Template and rules reference for the /ido4specs:synthesize-spec skill)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install ido4specs@claude-community` from `ido4-dev/ido4specs`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
